  "translations": {
    "Administrator's Guide": "",
    "Defining Storage Policies": "",
    "Defining your Storage Policies is very easy to do with Swift.  It is important that the administrator understand the concepts behind Storage Policies before actually creating and using them in order to get the most benefit out of the feature and, more importantly, to avoid having to make unnecessary changes once a set of policies have been deployed to a cluster.": "",
    "It is highly recommended that the reader fully read and comprehend :doc:`overview_policies` before proceeding with administration of policies.  Plan carefully and it is suggested that experimentation be done first on a non-production cluster to be certain that the desired configuration meets the needs of the users.  See :ref:`upgrade-policy` before planning the upgrade of your existing deployment.": "",
    "Following is a high level view of the very few steps it takes to configure policies once you have decided what you want to do:": "",
    "Define your policies in ``/etc/swift/swift.conf``": "SWIFT.conf 내에서 정책을 정의합니다.",
    "Create the corresponding object rings": "대응하는 객체 릴링크를 생성합니다.",
    "Communicate the names of the Storage Policies to cluster users": "스토리지 정책의 이름을 클러스터 사용자에게 공유합니다.",
    "For a specific example that takes you through these steps, please see :doc:`policies_saio`": "특수 예시가 있는 문서를 참조하여 이러한 단계를 통과해 주세요.",
    "Managing the Rings": "릴링크 관리를 합니다.",
    "You may build the storage rings on any server with the appropriate version of Swift installed.  Once built or changed (rebalanced), you must distribute the rings to all the servers in the cluster.  Storage rings contain information about all the Swift storage partitions and how they are distributed between the different nodes and disks.": "",
    "Swift 1.6.0 is the last version to use a Python pickle format. Subsequent versions use a different serialization format.  **Rings generated by Swift versions 1.6.0 and earlier may be read by any version, but rings generated after 1.6.0 may only be read by Swift versions greater than 1.6.0.**  So when upgrading from version 1.6.0 or earlier to a version greater than 1.6.0, either upgrade Swift on your ring building server **last** after all Swift nodes have been successfully upgraded, or refrain from generating rings until all Swift nodes have been successfully upgraded.": "",
    "If you need to downgrade from a version of Swift greater than 1.6.0 to a version less than or equal to 1.6.0, first downgrade your ring-building server, generate new rings, push them out, then continue with the rest of the downgrade.": "",
    "For more information see :doc:`overview_ring`.": "",
    "Removing a device from the ring::": "",
    "Removing a server from the ring::": "서버에서 립을 제거하기::",
    "Adding devices to the ring:": "서버에 장치 추가하기:",
    "See :ref:`ring-preparing`": "참조: 립 준비하기::",
    "See what devices for a server are in the ring::": "특정 서버의 장치가 립에 있는지 확인하기::",
    "Once you are done with all changes to the ring, the changes need to be \"committed\"::": "립 변경이 모두 완료되면 변경 사항이 \"시행\"되어야 합니다::",
    "Once the new rings are built, they should be pushed out to all the servers in the cluster.": "새로운 루그가 완성되면, 클러스터 내의 모든 서버에 그들을 push해야 합니다.",
    "Optionally, if invoked as 'swift-ring-builder-safe' the directory containing the specified builder file will be locked (via a .lock file in the parent directory). This provides a basic safe guard against multiple instances of the swift-ring-builder (or other utilities that observe this lock) from attempting to write to or read the builder/ring files while operations are in progress. This can be useful in environments where ring management has been automated but the operator still needs to interact with the rings manually.": "옵셔널: 지정된 밴더 파일이 있는 디렉토리에서 swift-ring-builder-safe를 호출하면 (상위 디렉토리의 부모 디렉토리에서 .lock 파일을 사용하여) 이 기본 안전 보호가 여러 instance의 swift-ring-builder 또는 다른 관찰하는 lock을 통해 빌더/라인 파일에 기록이나 읽기를 시도하려는 다른 utility를 방지합니다. 이것은 환경이 ring 관리를 자동화했지만 운영자만이 rings를 직접적으로 interacts 필요함을 여전히 제공합니다.",
    "If the ring builder is not producing the balances that you are expecting, you can gain visibility into what it's doing with the ``--debug`` flag.::": "빌더가 출력하는 균등성을 기대하고 있지 않다면, ``--debug`` 플래그를 사용하면 많은 출력 정보가 대부분의 루프 builder를 수정하려고 시도하거나 ring builder에 대해 보고서를 제출하려고 하는 경우 유용합니다.",
    "This produces a great deal of output that is mostly useful if you are either (a) attempting to fix the ring builder, or (b) filing a bug against the ring builder.": "이것은 병합 출력에서 'dispersion' 숫자를 만날 것입니다. 이 숫자가 의미하는 것은 :ref:`ring_dispersion`을 설명하고, 대략적으로는 각 익셉션 영역 안에 너무 많은 레 replication이 있는 ring의 일부 분할의 유형 비율입니다.",
    "You may notice in the rebalance output a 'dispersion' number. What this number means is explained in :ref:`ring_dispersion` but in essence is the percentage of partitions in the ring that have too many replicas within a particular failure domain. You can ask 'swift-ring-builder' what the dispersion is with::": "당신은 병합 출력에서 'dispersion' 숫자를 확인할 수 있습니다.",
    "This will give you the percentage again, if you want a detailed view of the dispersion simply add a ``--verbose``::": "이것은 당신이 dispersion의 상세한 시각을 원한다면 다시 주어질 양입니다. 단지 `--verbose`를 추가하면 더 상세한 분산 테이블이 표시됩니다, 이 테이블은 tier-by-tier 기준으로 디바이스 분산 정보를 제시합니다.",
    "This will not only display the percentage but will also display a dispersion table that lists partition dispersion by tier. You can use this table to figure out were you need to add capacity or to help tune an :ref:`ring_overload` value.": "이는 단순히 양을 표시하는 것 이상으로, dispersion 테이블을 포함하여 각 디바이스의 퍼센트와 분산을 표시하므로 capacity를 추가해야 하는지 및 ring_overload 값을 조정할 수 있는 예를 보여줍니다.",
    "Now let's take an example with 1 region, 3 zones and 4 devices. Each device has the same weight, and the ``dispersion --verbose`` might show the following::": "이제 1개의 지역, 3개의 구역, 그리고 4개의 장치로 가능한 예를 제안합니다. 각 디바이스가 동일한 가중치를 가지고 있으며, `dispersion --verbose`가 다음과 같이 나타낼 수 있습니다."
  }
}